# True Margin — Cursor Rules

## Context
Two-week overload-planning dashboard for Chatathon 2026 (WHOOP track).
The runnable demo is a single file: `index.html`. No backend, no
database, no live calendar required.

## The HTML Is The Product
`index.html` is the final UI. Keep README.md and DEMO_SCRIPT.md matched
to what this file actually does (Oracle Platform Engineering, Priya /
Amara, seed 4821, Thu 8 Architecture deep dive → Fri 9 10:30).
Do not resurrect a separate React app unless the user asks.

## Rule Engine Is Not AI
The logic in `analyseDay` / `recommend` must stay deterministic and fully
explainable in one sentence: if a meeting's concentration demand exceeds
the person's derived capacity in that block, flag it. Never replace this
with an ML model, embedding, or LLM call, and don't suggest doing so.

## Data Is Synthetic
`genData(seed)` builds the calendar, tasks, and check-ins. Don't connect
it to a real calendar API, database, or auth provider. Keep the
"Synthetic data — prototype" badge visible.

## Privacy Split
Manager view may show a 1–5 capacity band. It must never show energy,
meals, breaks, demand, or confidence answers. Those stay on the employee
Pulse / check-in screen.

## Scope Discipline
Out of scope for this repo: user authentication, a database, live
calendar integration, a server-side LLM proxy. Message drafts may *try*
a browser Claude call and must always fall back to the local template,
labelled on screen.

## Code Style
- One HTML file: vanilla JS + CSS in `index.html`
- No animation libraries — the UI needs to read clearly on a projector
- Both weeks and the recommendation card must stay on-screen at laptop
  and projector widths (no clipping the next week or the Apply actions)
- Comment any synthetic, simulated, or mocked behavior inline

## Protect the Happy Path
Every change should leave opening `index.html` working, seed 4821, and
the core flow intact: Amara → Thu 8 Overloaded → recommendation → Apply.
Flag any change that risks breaking it before applying.
